   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# AI Flotation Analyser  \n",
    "## Complete Feature Labelling, Exploratory Analysis, Feature Selection and Trial Model Training\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is designed to be both **runnable** and **explainable in a supervisor/client meeting**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What this notebook does\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Loads and audits the trial-level feature table.\n",
    "2. Separates **identifiers**, **quality-control variables**, and **behavioural variables**.\n",
    "3. Creates compact derived features such as mean arm and mean leg speed.\n",
    "4. Examines missing values and distributions.\n",
    "5. Produces a **correlation heatmap** and identifies redundant features.\n",
    "6. Standardises the compact behavioural feature set.\n",
    "7. Uses **PCA** to reduce correlated information.\n",
    "8. Checks several possible values of `k` using inertia and silhouette score.\n",
    "9. Fits an exploratory **K-means** clustering model.\n",
    "10. Visualises behavioural clusters in PCA space and compares cluster profiles.\n",
    "11. Uses the exploratory cluster as a **temporary target only** to test the supervised-learning pipeline.\n",
    "12. Compares a dummy baseline, Logistic Regression, Random Forest and Extra Trees.\n",
    "13. Reports **accuracy, balanced accuracy, precision, recall, F1 score and confusion matrix**.\n",
    "14. Calculates **permutation feature importance**.\n",
    "15. Performs **leave-one-feature-out ablation testing**.\n",
    "16. Creates a recommended feature-selection summary.\n",
    "17. Creates an expert-labelling template for the future real target.\n",
    "18. Contains a future-ready supervised section that automatically runs if expert labels are later supplied.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Important scientific limitation:** the temporary cluster label is derived from the same behavioural features used by the trial classifiers. Therefore, high classification performance only shows that the reduced features preserve the discovered behavioural grouping. It does **not** prove that the model predicts good or bad flotation. A real flotation-quality model requires an independent expert/domain label.\n"
   ]
  },
