    "\n",
    "## 3. Label the feature families\n",
    "\n",
    "Not every numeric column should be used as an ML predictor.\n",
    "\n",
    "We separate the columns conceptually into:\n",
    "\n",
    "### A. Identifiers / provenance\n",
    "Examples: participant ID, trial ID and source-video IDs.  \n",
    "These are useful for traceability and grouped validation but should **not** be learned as behavioural predictors.\n",
    "\n",
    "### B. Quality-control variables\n",
    "Examples: pose coverage percentages and torso size in pixels.  \n",
    "These help us decide whether a trial is sufficiently reliable, but they are not direct measures of flotation behaviour.\n",
    "\n",
    "### C. Behavioural variables\n",
    "These describe posture, whole-body drift, arm activity and leg activity. These are the variables we investigate as candidate predictors.\n"
   ]
