    "\n",
    "## 8. Correlation analysis and redundancy\n",
    "\n",
    "Many raw measurements describe very similar movement.\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples include:\n",
    "\n",
    "- path distance and average speed,\n",
    "- left and right limb activity,\n",
    "- average speed and high-percentile speed.\n",
    "\n",
    "We use **Spearman correlation** because it measures monotonic association and is less dependent on normal-distribution assumptions than Pearson correlation.\n",
    "\n",
    "A correlation near `+1` or `-1` means two variables carry highly overlapping information. This does **not** automatically mean one must be deleted, but it is a warning that the feature set may be unnecessarily repetitive.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e015901d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
