    "\n",
    "## 9. Why the six-feature compact set is used first\n",
    "\n",
    "The initial six features are intentionally simple and interpretable:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Feature | Behaviour represented |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Typical trunk angle | Typical body orientation |\n",
    "| Trunk-angle IQR | Postural variability/stability |\n",
    "| Maximum body excursion | Largest whole-body movement away from the reference position |\n",
    "| Body path rate | Rate of whole-body movement |\n",
    "| Mean arm speed | Overall arm activity |\n",
    "| Mean leg speed | Overall leg activity |\n",
    "\n",
    "The goal is to avoid letting many near-duplicate measurements dominate PCA, clustering or later supervised models.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a95dcbe9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
