   "source": [
    "\n",
    "## 10. Standardisation\n",
    "\n",
    "PCA and K-means are distance/variance-based methods.\n",
    "\n",
    "The features are measured in different units:\n",
    "\n",
    "- degrees,\n",
    "- torso lengths,\n",
    "- torso lengths per second.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, each feature is standardised to approximately mean `0` and standard deviation `1`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Without standardisation, a feature with numerically larger values could influence the result mainly because of its scale.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "007dbc95",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "X = df[CORE_FEATURES].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X)\n",
    "\n",
    "scaled_df = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "    X_scaled,\n",
    "    columns=CORE_FEATURES,\n",
    "    index=df.index,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "display(scaled_df.describe().round(3))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d8600a3b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "## 11. Principal Component Analysis (PCA)\n",
    "\n",
    "PCA converts correlated input features into new orthogonal components.\n",
    "\n",
    "We inspect:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. the variance explained by each component,\n",
    "2. cumulative explained variance,\n",
    "3. and feature loadings.\n",
    "\n",
    "The first few components can then summarise the dominant behavioural patterns without repeatedly weighting highly related variables.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "acc95369",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
