    "\n",
    "## 15. Clustering robustness check with Ward hierarchical clustering\n",
    "\n",
    "K-means is only one clustering algorithm.\n",
    "\n",
    "As a simple robustness check, we also create three clusters using Ward hierarchical clustering and compare the two assignments with the **Adjusted Rand Index (ARI)**.\n",
    "\n",
    "- ARI near `1` = strong agreement.\n",
    "- ARI near `0` = agreement similar to chance.\n",
    "- Negative ARI = worse than chance agreement.\n",
    "\n",
    "This does not prove that the clusters are \"true\", but stronger agreement suggests that the overall structure is not unique to one clustering method.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "61a0c0d0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "ward_linkage = linkage(X_pca3, method=\"ward\")\n",
    "ward_labels = fcluster(\n",
    "    ward_linkage,\n",
    "    t=3,\n",
    "    criterion=\"maxclust\",\n",
    ") - 1\n",
    "\n",
    "ari_kmeans_ward = adjusted_rand_score(cluster_id, ward_labels)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Adjusted Rand Index: K-means vs Ward clustering = {ari_kmeans_ward:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"trial_id\": df[\"trial_id\"],\n",
    "    \"kmeans_cluster\": cluster_id,\n",
    "    \"ward_cluster\": ward_labels,\n",
    "}).to_csv(\n",
    "    OUTPUT_DIR / \"kmeans_vs_ward_cluster_assignments.csv\",\n",
    "    index=False,\n",
    ")\n"
   ]
